      "reviewed": "2026-11-03",
      "notes": "One zip per municipality, shapefile edition: shapefiles/l3parcels/L3_SHP_M###_NAME.zip in the public bucket download.massgis.digital.mass.gov, read through the S3 REST endpoint s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com (the website alias download.massgis.digital.mass.gov does not answer HTTPS). Each zip holds the Assess table as a dBase file (M###Assess_CY##_FY##.dbf, owner names included), a use-code lookup (M###UC_LUT), and the parcel shapefiles. These 176 files are the municipalities of Middlesex (54), Worcester (60), Essex (34) and Norfolk (28) counties; the bucket lists 351 towns (about 935 MB in all; the four counties are about 515 MB; the largest file here is 13.5 MB; Boston's is 31 MB and is covered by ma-boston-assessing). Town files are refreshed on the towns' own schedules (the 2026-10-30 list shows dates from 2021 to 2026), so re-run discover/snapshot weekly and the collector keeps only changed files. Aggregate statewide geodatabases (L3_AGGREGATE_FGDB_*.zip, 7-8.5 GB) are NOT used. robots.txt: the S3 endpoint answers 403 AccessDenied to /robots.txt, which the collector reads as no rules; the mass.gov pages (terms_url, the MassGIS data page) answer the collector with 403 'Not allowed' and could not be read by it, so the licence text above was read from the metadata packed in the downloads themselves. Bucket listing used for discovery: https://s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/download.massgis.digital.mass.gov?list-type=2&prefix=shapefiles/l3parcels/L3_SHP_M . Landing page: the bucket's S3 listing for the l3parcels prefix (mass.gov answers the collector with 403, so its page cannot be the landing page); the town files are listed explicitly."
